# ===========================================================================
# SDC (Skilleddesk Code) — environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what your machine needs:
#
#   PowerShell :  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#   bash/zsh   :  cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is ignored by git (see .gitignore §1). This file holds no values, and
# that is the rule that keeps it safe to publish: variable NAMES and comments
# belong in the repository, VALUES never do.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What SDC actually reads from the environment
#
# Almost nothing, by design. The app's configuration is its own store, and
# provider credentials belong in the OS keychain rather than in a file — the
# provider hub of spec §9.10 stores keys in the platform keychain, and CLI
# engines (`claude`, `codex`, `gemini`) keep their own logins. So there is no
# `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` contract here to fill in.
#
# The variables below exist only for local development. Anything not listed is
# not read by any code in this repository.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Desktop shell / Vite dev server  (read by app/vite.config.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set by the Tauri CLI when developing against a device or VM (mobile targets,
# a remote Linux box, a Windows VM). Left empty for ordinary desktop work, where
# the dev server binds to localhost on port 1420.
#
# Setting it by hand points the dev server at a LAN address; it is a Node-side
# variable, so it never reaches the frontend bundle.
TAURI_DEV_HOST=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend variables — read the warning before adding one
#
# Vite inlines every variable prefixed with `VITE_` into the built JavaScript.
# That bundle ships to end users and is trivially readable, so a `VITE_` value is
# public by definition. Never put a key, token, password or endpoint secret here;
# if you need one of those, it belongs behind the daemon, not in the UI.
#
# VITE_EXAMPLE_PUBLIC_FLAG=0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional, local experiments only
#
# Uncommenting any of these puts a live credential in a file on disk. Prefer the
# provider hub (spec §9.10) or the engine's own login instead. If you do use one,
# make sure `.env` stays untracked (`git status --porcelain .env` must be empty)
# and rotate the key afterwards.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#
# A local Ollama instance, if it is not on the default port:
# OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Daemon (`sdcd/`) — none yet
#
# The host daemon takes its configuration from its own files, not from the
# environment. When it grows environment-driven settings they are added here
# with an empty value and a comment saying what reads them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
